{"v":1,"agent":"copilot-cli","cli_version":"0.10.3","type":"assistant","ts":"2026-09-01T21:51:09.022Z","id":"9f54d0f2-f6f8-465d-b4e2-1dd7cc9a262e","content":[{"text":"That rule is VitePress's default theme style (`vitepress/dist/client/theme-default/styles/base.css`), which applies **only to the host page's `\u003cbody\u003e`** in the outer document, not inside the demo iframe.\n\n### How the demo iframe isolation works\n\n1. **Two-layer iframe sandbox:**\n   - **Outer frame** ([tools/demo/runner/index.html](tools/demo/runner/index.html)): Loads `/play/index.html` with its own isolated stylesheet ([tools/demo/runner/runner.css](tools/demo/runner/runner.css)).\n   - **Inner frame** ([tools/demo/runner/main.ts](tools/demo/runner/main.ts#L321-L326)): Renders the demo via a sandboxed `\u003ciframe class=\"runner__result\" srcdoc=\"...\"\u003e`.\n2. **CSS isolation:**\n   - `srcdoc` creates an isolated document tree. Styles from the parent document (such as VitePress's `body` rule, `.vp-doc`, and `--vp-c-*` variables) cannot pierce the iframe boundary.\n   - The stylesheets injected into the demo (`cssUrls`) only include Instructure token and component sheets (`base.css`, `components.css`, `site-themes.css`, etc.)—none contain `--vp-c-bg` or VitePress rules.\n3. **Background hierarchy in the runner:**\n   - **Inner iframe `\u003chtml\u003e`**: Sets `background: var(--instui-color-background-page)` from [formats/components/src/rules/base/base.css](formats/components/src/rules/base/base.css#L22).\n   - **Inner iframe `\u003cbody\u003e`**: Defaults to `margin: 0; padding: var(--instui-spacing-space-md, 1rem);` with no background set (transparent, showing the `\u003chtml\u003e` page background).\n   - **Demo CSS** ([docs/demos/pendo/style.css](docs/demos/pendo/style.css)): Injected into the inner iframe's `\u003chead\u003e\u003cstyle\u003e` block, so any background defined on `body`, `html`, or `.pendo-showcase` applies directly to the demo.\n\nIf DevTools displayed `body { background-color: var(--vp-c-bg); ... }`, DevTools had the top-level host page's `\u003cbody\u003e` selected rather than the nested `#document \u003e html \u003e body` inside `iframe.pantoken-demo__frame` $\\rightarrow$ `iframe.runner__result`.","type":"text"}]}
